{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793741648,"nonce":"djvjiy9zndb1hmMdA1WnhCEO/S4=","message":"Implemented lazy bytecode call-site symbol caching with registration-generation invalidation. Positive results are cached only for executed sites; missing symbols remain retryable. Public typed/untyped registrations and replacement of shared tables invalidate entries; binding the identical shared table preserves them. An untouched symbol pool allocates no cache and never initializes the shared symbol table. Native tiering policy and GC behavior are unchanged.\n\nNUC release LLVM-enabled build, pure HIR interpreter microbenchmarks (no JIT hooks), affinity 0,2,4,6. Fifteen alternating baseline/candidate rounds, 100000 warm calls per shape; no Cargo/rustc during or between samples. Cold bytecode benchmark: 1000 freshly constructed interpreters, registration outside timed interval. Scalar control: 1000000 loop iterations. All checksums/assertions passed. Medians in nanoseconds:\nroots=false,symbols=1: 138.00 -\u003e 103.22 (1.337x)\nroots=false,symbols=24: 661.27 -\u003e 211.05 (3.133x)\nroots=true,symbols=1: 181.79 -\u003e 151.76 (1.198x)\nroots=true,symbols=24: 703.95 -\u003e 257.66 (2.732x)\ncold_symbols=24: 9440.89 -\u003e 9060.00 (1.042x)\nscalar_iteration: 41.23 -\u003e 41.42 (0.995x)\n\nThese are interpreter microbenchmarks, not whole-program Lua/Python speedups. Matched-workload perf samples put about 48% of baseline CPU in symbol lookup/hash/compare; those functions fall below the 1% display threshold in the candidate. Register initialization, cloning/drops, call setup, allocation and GC root registration dominate the remainder. Follow-ups: 693a5fd for frame/argument storage and 1f4d901 for compact scalar registers/bytecode. The existing 9a71873 tracks native-call stack clearing.\n\nBaseline source c53620ef0c05e161afb92fe8f8328b89ed6ece63. Baseline executable SHA256 483669c3e8ab3c782fbd1b82f5b14c0b7425d25933870a4ca281ebc6681c5515. Candidate executable SHA256 3b5471d44a3dea6343f43adf25e6cb0a2b2a71579a77d0c7f2275886ca2b2601. Rust 1.101.0-nightly (c36f14571 2026-10-01), LLVM21. Five targeted tests pass on the NUC; existing recursion/OSR checks and the targeted tests pass on arm64. Clippy relevant compiler library/test with warnings denied passes. Complete pinned TS corpus and frontend execution fixtures are being checked before commit.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/zyntax-interpreter-speed/{results.json,base-final-profile.txt,candidate-profile.txt,tests.log}. NUC original HEAD, tracked diff and untracked contents restored exactly and preservation stash dropped. Task scratch cleaned after evidence copied.","files":null}]}